                       "id":  "ingles-106",
                       "texto_apoio":  "Ordinary people around the world are contributing to real scientific research by counting birds in their backyards, photographing plants for identification apps, or reporting weather observations. These citizen science projects have allowed researchers to gather data across enormous geographic areas that would be impossible to cover with professional scientists alone.",
