                       "id":  "ingles-109",
                       "texto_apoio":  "Wearable devices that track heart rate, sleep patterns, and physical activity have become increasingly popular among people trying to monitor their own health. Doctors note that while these devices can help users notice unusual patterns early, the data should not replace professional medical evaluation, since consumer devices are not always as accurate as clinical equipment.",
