                       "texto_apoio":  "Marine biologists have discovered that the constant low-frequency noise produced by cargo ships travels enormous distances underwater, overlapping with the frequencies whales use to communicate over long ranges. In busy shipping lanes, some whale populations have been observed calling more loudly and for longer periods, which researchers believe consumes extra energy the animals need for feeding and migration.",
