                       "id":  "ingles-132",
                       "texto_apoio":  "Consumer advocates have long criticized manufacturers for designing products, from smartphones to household appliances, that are difficult or impossible to repair and that stop receiving software updates after just a few years, forcing customers to buy replacements far sooner than necessary. Some manufacturers deny doing this deliberately, attributing shorter product lifespans to genuine technical limitations.",
